{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"allstar-sleepy-armadillo","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Observation\nA sandboxed local `make verify` (worktree almondy-drop-acl-step, Nov 19 18:23 to Nov 20 01:14 PST, tree origin/main 717c50f8b33 plus a workflow-only change) failed `tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_atomic_completion_close.py::test_two_processes_publish_at_most_one_equivalent_same_ticket_bundle` at `ProcessPoolExecutor(max_workers=2)` (test line 399) with `PermissionError: [Errno 1] Operation not permitted`, raised from CPython 3.12 `concurrent/futures/process.py:613`. That line is `os.sysconf(\"SC_SEM_NSEMS_MAX\")` in `_check_system_limits`, which catches only AttributeError and ValueError. The same change passed CI Verified (Gerrit 3475, run 44732620097).\n\nThe test carries `@pytest.mark.requires_posix_named_semaphore`, whose conftest hook skips it (counted) when `tests/_sandbox_capabilities.posix_named_semaphore_probe()` reports unavailable. That probe only constructs a `_multiprocessing.SemLock`.\n\nMeasured 2026-11-20 on this host, same interpreter: inside the Claude Code sandbox the probe returns `available=True`, `os.sysconf(\"SC_SEM_NSEMS_MAX\")` raises `PermissionError [Errno 1]`, and `ProcessPoolExecutor(1)` raises the same error. Outside the sandbox sysconf returns 87381 and the pool runs. So the failure is deterministic under the sandbox and is not load-related.\n\n## Root cause\nThe probe checks a different capability from the one the marked tests need: the sandbox allows SemLock creation but denies the sysconf query that ProcessPoolExecutor makes first. The marker therefore does not skip a test the host cannot run.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] The probe reports unavailable when `os.sysconf(\"SC_SEM_NSEMS_MAX\")` raises OSError, with a unit test for that branch through an injected sysconf.\n- [ ] Inside the agent sandbox the atomic-close test is a counted skip rather than a failure; outside it, it still runs and passes.","id":"fa59-9a21-097b-49be","parent_id":"","priority":3,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Semaphore capability probe passes in the agent sandbox, but ProcessPoolExecutor still fails on os.sysconf EPERM"},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1795179068115601001,"uuid":"7ac2eef9-6da1-41f1-a51a-8afc9b0a2460"}